   listening preference (she listens in book order), never
   a system or gate dependency. Its job is `parked_policy`; **how a parked
   job resumes mechanically must be verified as that
   gate's first step** (this proposal deliberately proves
   nothing about the resume mechanism, only that re-arm
   doesn't touch it). Book-scope quotes for the generation
   gate exclude Chapter 3's 24 parked occurrences, as
   before.
3. **Batch arming** remains its own decision, unmade.

---

## 11. Decision point for Rowan

**DP-C1 — playback-surface snapshot verification in the
armed-idle read set.** Gate (a)'s D4 verification (a *code
deploy*) compared the content/bindings snapshot heads
digest-for-digest. Gate-7's A5/A6 (the only other
metadata-only flip) did **not** — its read set was state
surfaces only. **Wren's lean: follow Gate-7 — do NOT add
snapshot-digest comparison to §6's read set.** Reasons:
(i) the flip changes no code bytes, and R3 proves that
strictly — parts byte-identical to the manifest + etag
unchanged is *stronger* evidence the playback surface is
untouched than a snapshot digest comparison would be;
(ii) the read set already includes both watermark counters
(content 18 / bindings 1818), which move on any
content/bindings write — a snapshot *write* cannot hide
from them; (iii) precedent: the one prior execution of
this exact mechanism is the controlling pattern, and
deviating needs a reason this build supplies none of.
If Rowan prefers the belt-and-braces version, adding the
two snapshot-head digests to the read set is a one-line
amendment Wren will make without further reference to
Julie (it changes no scope — reads only).

No other forks are open. Everything else is fixed by the
rulings and precedents cited in the source index.

